  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Eight in a row, and they never trailed once.",
    "what_this_means": "They led from the first inning at Coors and didn't give it back. Merrill and France both went 3-for-5, and the lineup scraped together 13 hits into eight runs. Not pretty, not overwhelming, but enough to hold a five-run margin through nine innings. Mize surrendered only two runs across five innings, then the bullpen held the line when it mattered. Rodriguez bridged into the seventh with a clean 1.2 innings. Morejon got his inning. Mason Miller came in cold and struck out two for the save. This is what a complete game looks like when nothing breaks your concentration. Pitching steady, offense finding gaps, bullpen not making you older. The formula is working because both sides are clicking at the same time. That doesn't last forever.",
    "what_to_watch": "Freeland has a 6.37 ERA and the Padres send Buehler to the mound tonight with his line solid at 3.48 over his last four starts.",
